# Rendered for the mt2009 stack by linux-port-mt2009/port/envify.py from
# linux-port/docker/.env.example, plus the keys only this stack reads,
# which are edited here and kept by the render (see envify.py).
# =============================================================================
#  Metin2 server -- configuration.
#
#  Copy this file to `.env' and edit it:
#
#      cp .env.example .env
#      nano .env
#
#  Only the first two sections need your attention. Everything else has a
#  working default and can be left exactly as it is.
#
#  `.env' contains your passwords. Do not commit it and do not paste it into
#  a forum post when asking for help.
# =============================================================================


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  1. REQUIRED -- the server will not start without these
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The address players type into their client. Your VPS's public IP address, or
# a domain name pointing at it.
#
# This is the single most important setting. Without it, players reach the
# login screen, log in successfully, and then hang forever on "connecting to
# the server" -- because the login server hands out an address that only exists
# inside the container.
#
# Find your VPS's public address with:   curl -4 ifconfig.me
# PL: adres, ktory gracze wpisuja w kliencie. Na wlasnym komputerze zostaw
#      pusty (launcher wpisze 127.0.0.1); na VPS wpisz publiczny adres IP
#      albo domene, bo inaczej gracze zawisna na "laczenie z serwerem".
M2_PUBLIC_ADDRESS=

# Database passwords. Invent two long random ones; you will not need to type
# them again. Generate them with:   openssl rand -hex 24
#
# No spaces and no double quotes -- the game's config parser splits on those.
# Keep them under 120 characters.
# PL: haslo administratora bazy danych. Instalator wpisuje je sam. Zmien tylko
#      razem z drugim haslem i tylko przed pierwszym startem - pozniejsza
#      zmiana odetnie serwer od jego wlasnej bazy.
M2_DB_ROOT_PASSWORD=
# PL: haslo uzytkownika bazy, ktorego uzywa serwer gry. Jak wyzej: ustawiane
#      raz, przy instalacji.
M2_DB_PASSWORD=

# Host port for local database tools (Navicat, HeidiSQL, DBeaver). The database
# is published only on 127.0.0.1 at this port, so connect to 127.0.0.1:3306 with
# user root (M2_DB_ROOT_PASSWORD) or metin2 (M2_DB_PASSWORD). Change it if 3306
# is already used by another MySQL/MariaDB.
# PL: port, na ktorym baza jest widoczna dla HeidiSQL/Navicata na tym komputerze
#      (127.0.0.1:3306). Zmien, jesli masz juz inna baze MySQL na 3306.
M2_DB_PUBLISH_PORT=3306


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  2. RECOMMENDED
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The password you will use to log in to the admin panel.
# Leave it EMPTY and one will be generated for you and printed once, on the
# panel's first start:   docker compose logs panel | grep -A4 PASSWORD
#
# Changing this later has no effect on its own -- the panel keeps its password
# in a config file created on first run. To change it:
#     docker compose exec panel rm /usr/local/etc/m2panel.conf
#     docker compose restart panel
# Whether the panel asks for the passphrase at all. On this line empty (the
# default) opens it without one on any address: the 2.x suite is a world for
# one player at their own machine. A server anybody else can reach - a VPS,
# a forwarded port, a proxy in front - sets 0 here and a M2_PANEL_PASSWORD,
# or keeps the panels on 127.0.0.1 (M2_PANEL_BIND_ADDRESS) and opens them
# through an SSH tunnel. The advanced panel (7790) has its own switch in its
# settings and starts without a passphrase too. 1 forces the open panel.
# PL: na linii 2.x panel domyslnie NIE pyta o haslo, na zadnym adresie (to
#      swiat dla jednego gracza). Na VPS albo przy przekierowanym porcie
#      ustaw tu 0 i haslo w M2_PANEL_PASSWORD - albo trzymaj panele na
#      127.0.0.1 (M2_PANEL_BIND_ADDRESS) i otwieraj je przez tunel SSH.
#      Panel zaawansowany (7790) tez startuje bez hasla; wlacza sie je w
#      jego ustawieniach. 1 = zawsze bez hasla.
M2_PANEL_LOCAL_ONLY=

# PL: haslo do panelu. Puste i panel wymyka wlasne przy pierwszym starcie -
#      wpisz tu swoje, jesli chcesz je znac z gory.
M2_PANEL_PASSWORD=

# Your timezone. The server names its log directories by local date and the
# panel shows the containers' clock, so getting this right keeps both lined up
# with yours. Left at UTC, the launcher sets it once to the Windows zone (and
# linux-port/tools/update.sh, run on a Linux host, to the host's); what you set
# after that is kept.
# Full list:  https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_tz_database_time_zones
# PL: strefa czasowa kontenerow, np. Europe/Warsaw. Ustawia godziny w logach,
#      w panelu i w nocy botow. Launcher wpisuje tu strefe Windowsa.
M2_TZ=UTC

# Server-side item, monster and quest text used for a fresh language state.
# Available codes depend on the supplied r40250 pack (usually en/pl/de/etc.).
# A later choice made in the panel is persistent and takes priority.
# PL: jezyk nazw w grze: pl albo en. Przelacza sie tez przyciskiem w panelu.
M2_DEFAULT_GAME_LANGUAGE=en

# The name shown on the panel's public page.
# PL: nazwa serwera pokazywana w panelu i na stronie. Puste = nazwa domyslna.
M2_BRAND=

# Where players download your game client from, if you host it elsewhere.
# Leave empty to serve it from the panel itself -- which is what the client
# builder below fills in for you.
# PL: adres, spod ktorego panel proponuje pobranie klienta. Dla wlasnego
#      serwera zwykle niepotrzebne.
M2_CLIENT_URL=
# PL: nazwa pliku klienta pokazywana graczom przy pobieraniu.
M2_CLIENT_NAME=


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  2b. The game client players download
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The panel has a "Download the game" button. It is dead until there is a client
# to hand out. Build one -- once -- with:
#
#     docker compose run --rm client-builder
#
# The builder needs an archive you supplied in ./client-archive/ or an explicit
# M2_CLIENT_ARCHIVE_URL that you are authorised to use. The project has no
# built-in mirror. It writes your address into that client and puts the result
# where the panel serves it; cached local archives are not downloaded twice.

# The address baked into the client. Empty means "use M2_PUBLIC_ADDRESS", which
# is right on a VPS and right for a local install (127.0.0.1). Set it only when
# the two must differ -- for instance when the server is reached through a
# hostname you have not put in M2_PUBLIC_ADDRESS.
# PL: adres, ktory launcher wpisuje klientowi do serverinfo. Puste = to, co
#      stoi w M2_PUBLIC_ADDRESS.
M2_CLIENT_ADDRESS=

# The name players see in the client's server list. Empty uses the name the
# server files ship with ("Singleplayer Official Metin2").
# PL: nazwa serwera na liscie w kliencie.
M2_CLIENT_SERVER_NAME=

# These follow M2_CHANNELS and M2_AUTH_PORT above. Only set them if the client
# has to be told something different from what this stack runs -- which is
# almost always a mistake: a channel the client lists but the server does not
# run looks to a player exactly like a broken server.
# PL: ile kanalow klient ma pokazac na liscie. Puste = tyle, ile naprawde stoi.
M2_CLIENT_CHANNELS=
# PL: port logowania wpisywany klientowi. Puste = M2_AUTH_PORT.
M2_CLIENT_AUTH_PORT=

# Prefer putting your compatible archive in ./client-archive/. Alternatively,
# give the builder an explicit operator-owned direct/MEGA URL here.
# PL: skad launcher sciaga paczke klienta. Zostaw puste - adres wydania jest
#      brany z manifestu.
M2_CLIENT_ARCHIVE_URL=

# The same archive somewhere else. Tried in order when the link above will not
# come -- above all when MEGA answers "509 over quota", which is the share
# owner's daily allowance being spent and has nothing to do with this machine.
# The installer fills these in from artifacts.json; a link put here by hand
# wins over that.
# PL: adres zapasowy paczki klienta, gdy glowny nie odpowiada.
M2_CLIENT_ARCHIVE_URL_FALLBACK=
# PL: drugi adres zapasowy paczki klienta.
M2_CLIENT_ARCHIVE_URL_FALLBACK2=

# If you know the archive's SHA-256, put it here and it will be checked before
# anything is built from it. Leave empty and the archive is checked for
# truncation instead, which is the failure that actually happens.
# PL: suma kontrolna paczki klienta. Puste = sprawdzana z manifestu.
M2_CLIENT_ARCHIVE_SHA256=

# Keep the downloaded archive after the client is built. 1 (the default) costs
# about 1.4 GB of disk and means a rebuild never needs the network. Set it to 0
# on a small VPS: re-addressing the client stays free either way, only a full
# rebuild would download again.
# PL: czy zachowac pobrany zip klienta po rozpakowaniu. 1 = tak (szybsza
#      naprawa), 0 = skasuj i odzyskaj miejsce.
M2_CLIENT_KEEP_ARCHIVE=1

# How much free disk to insist on before starting. The archive, the client
# inside it, the unpacked tree and the new zip briefly exist at once.
# PL: ile megabajtow wolnego miejsca musi byc, zeby zaczac pobieranie klienta.
M2_CLIENT_MIN_FREE_MB=7000


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  3. Server shape -- safe to leave alone
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# How many channels to run. Each channel is three game cores using roughly
# 320 + 300 + 240 MB of RAM, so one channel needs ~1 GB and four need ~3.5 GB.
# One channel is right for anything under a few hundred players.
#
# IMPORTANT: channel N listens on 13000+10*(N-1) .. +2 inside the container, and
# compose publishes M2_GAME_PORT_RANGE (host) onto M2_GAME_CONTAINER_PORT_RANGE
# (container) - widen BOTH, to the same length, or the extra channels run and
# nobody can reach them:
#   1 channel  -> 13000-13002
#   2 channels -> 13000-13012
#   3 channels -> 13000-13022
#   4 channels -> 13000-13032
# Bots only ever play on the first two, and only with M2_PLAYERBOT_CH2 below;
# a channel the bots do not use is a players' channel.
# PL: ile kanalow gry ma wstac. Dla drugiego kanalu uzyj M2_PLAYERBOT_CH2=1,
#      ktory ustawi to sam razem z portami.
M2_CHANNELS=1
# PL: porty gry otwierane na tym komputerze. 13000-13002 to jeden kanal,
#      13000-13012 to dwa. Ustawiane automatycznie przy wlaczaniu kanalu.
M2_GAME_PORT_RANGE=13000-13002
# PL: to samo po stronie kontenera - oba zakresy musza byc rowne.
M2_GAME_CONTAINER_PORT_RANGE=13000-13002

# The login port. Change only if something else on the VPS already uses 11000;
# players would then have to be told the new port.
# PL: port logowania. Zmien, jesli 11000 jest zajety przez inny program.
M2_AUTH_PORT=11000

# The numeric port the admin panel is reachable on: http://<your-ip>:7788
# Put the bind address in M2_PANEL_BIND_ADDRESS, not on this line.
# Set it to 80 to serve the panel on the normal web port.
# PL: port panelu klasycznego (http://127.0.0.1:7788).
M2_PANEL_PUBLIC_PORT=7788

# Seban's panel (the second web view: map, profiles, rankings, economy,
# grants). Its port on this machine; 7789 belongs to the browser bridge.
# PL: port panelu zaawansowanego (http://127.0.0.1:7790).
M2_SEBAN_PANEL_PORT=7790
# Its session secret. Leave empty and the admin-page secret above is used.
# PL: klucz sesji panelu zaawansowanego. Puste = losowany przy starcie.
M2_SEBAN_SESSION_SECRET=

# The ItemShop (Dragon Coins / Dragon Marks), opened from the coin on the
# game's taskbar. Its port on this machine.
# PL: port sklepu z przedmiotami (ItemShop).
M2_ITEMSHOP_PUBLIC_PORT=7791
# The address the game sends the player's client to, as host:port without
# http://. Leave empty to use M2_PUBLIC_ADDRESS and the port above.
# PL: adres ItemShopu, ktory gra podaje klientowi po komendzie /mall.
M2_MALL_URL=
# The address of the classic panel as the visitor's browser reaches it, for
# the link and the skill icons. Empty means http://127.0.0.1:<panel port>.
# PL: adres panelu klasycznego widoczny w panelu zaawansowanym (przycisk
#      przejscia miedzy panelami).
M2_SEBAN_TIERU_PANEL_URL=

# Maximum character level. 120 is the highest the game can do at all
# (PLAYER_MAX_LEVEL_CONST); this is where you decide how much of that to use.
#
# The panel reads the same number, so its "set level" box offers exactly what
# the server accepts. That is not cosmetic: the server does not refuse a level
# above this one, it silently ignores it and reports success, so before the
# panel knew the limit you could set 110, be told it worked, and find the
# character still at its old level.
# PL: maksymalny poziom postaci na serwerze.
M2_MAX_LEVEL=120

# How many Playerbots the game cores start, split equally between the three
# kingdoms. The seed holds 1500 a kingdom (PID 4..4503, since 2.2.1) and the
# ceiling is 2500. Start with 10-25 while debugging a new client or map.
# PL: ILU BOTOW MA GRAC. Najczesciej zmieniana linia w tym pliku. Suwak w
#      launcherze ustawia to samo. Wiecej botow to wiecej zycia w swiecie i
#      wieksze obciazenie procesora; 350 to spokojny domyslny swiat, 1000
#      wymaga juz mocniejszej maszyny.
PLAYERBOT_AUTOSPAWN_COUNT=350

# Stali dropiacy medali: tylu botow NA KAZDE krolestwo ponad PLAYERBOT_AUTOSPAWN_COUNT
# (0 = wylaczone). Maja osobowosc "dropek medali": chodza do Lochu Malp swojego
# krolestwa, a od PLAYERBOT_MEDAL_DROPPER_LEVEL (co najmniej 18) nie zdobywaja juz
# doswiadczenia, wiec medale padaja im na pelnej szansie i trafiaja na straganach
# do botow, ktore same z lochu juz nie wyjda. Wybierani z najmlodszych postaci
# kazdego krolestwa, co restart ci sami.
# PL: ilu botow na krolestwo ma byc "dropkami medali" - siedza w Lochu Malp i
#      farmia medale konne na sprzedaz. 0 = wylaczone.
PLAYERBOT_MEDAL_DROPPERS=0
# PL: na jakim poziomie zablokowac dropki medali (18-120). Niski poziom to
#      lepszy drop medalu, bo szansa spada z roznicy poziomow.
PLAYERBOT_MEDAL_DROPPER_LEVEL=25

# Stopniowe wpuszczanie botow. PLAYERBOT_AUTOSPAWN_COUNT botow wchodzi w ciagu
# PLAYERBOT_SPAWN_WINDOW_MINUTES minut od startu (1 = jak dotad, do 180), a
# PLAYERBOT_LATE_JOINERS dodatkowych dolacza pojedynczo, rownomiernie w ciagu
# PLAYERBOT_LATE_JOIN_HOURS godzin (1-168). Np. 1000 botow w 15 minut i 500
# kolejnych w ciagu doby: 1000 / 15 / 500 / 24. Launcher: LICZBA BOTOW.
# PL: przez ile minut boty maja sie logowac po starcie serwera. 1 = wszystkie
#      naraz (tlok na placu), 10 = wchodza stopniowo.
PLAYERBOT_SPAWN_WINDOW_MINUTES=1
# PL: ilu dodatkowych botow ma dolaczac pozniej, juz w trakcie gry. 0 = nikt.
PLAYERBOT_LATE_JOINERS=0
# PL: przez ile godzin maja sie rozlozyc te pozniejsze dolaczenia.
PLAYERBOT_LATE_JOIN_HOURS=24

# Osobna liczba botow dla kazdego krolestwa zamiast jednej liczby dzielonej po
# rowno (launcher: LICZBA BOTOW -> "Indywidualne wartosci dla krolestw").
# 1 = kazde krolestwo startuje tyle botow, ile tu podano (najwyzej tyle, ile ma
# postaci - od 2.2.1 po 1500), a PLAYERBOT_AUTOSPAWN_COUNT jest wtedy pomijany.
# PL: 1 = podaj liczbe botow osobno dla kazdego krolestwa w trzech liniach
#      ponizej; 0 = jedna liczba z PLAYERBOT_AUTOSPAWN_COUNT dzielona po rowno.
PLAYERBOT_AUTOSPAWN_PER_KINGDOM=0
# PL: ilu botow w Shinsoo (dziala przy PLAYERBOT_AUTOSPAWN_PER_KINGDOM=1).
PLAYERBOT_AUTOSPAWN_SHINSOO=0
# PL: ilu botow w Chunjo (jak wyzej).
PLAYERBOT_AUTOSPAWN_CHUNJO=0
# PL: ilu botow w Jinno (jak wyzej).
PLAYERBOT_AUTOSPAWN_JINNO=0

# Drugi kanal (CH2) dla botow i graczy, domyslnie wylaczony. Wlaczony: serwer
# uruchamia drugi kanal (trzy kolejne rdzenie gry, ~1 GB RAM), PLAYERBOT_CH2_SHARE
# procent botow gra na CH2, a reszta na CH1 - kazdy bot zawsze na jednym i tym
# samym kanale. Wszystkie sklepy (botow i graczy) stoja tylko na CH1; bot, ktory
# kiedykolwiek mial sklep, zostaje na CH1 na stale. Wlaczaj z launchera (LICZBA
# BOTOW) albo w panelu WWW (Stawki): launcher otwiera wtedy porty 13010-13012
# (M2_GAME_PORT_RANGE i M2_GAME_CONTAINER_PORT_RANGE = 13000-13012).
# M2_PLAYERBOT_CH2_SET_AT to chwila ostatniej zmiany - nowsze z dwojga, .env albo
# ustawienie z panelu WWW, wygrywa przy starcie serwera.
# PL: drugi kanal gry: 1 = wlacz, 0 = jeden kanal. Wlaczenie otwiera tez porty
#      13010-13012. Wlacza sie tez przyciskiem w panelu.
M2_PLAYERBOT_CH2=0
# PL: jaki procent botow ma grac na drugim kanale (10-90). Boty ze straganami
#      i tak wracaja na pierwszy, bo tam stoja sklepy.
PLAYERBOT_CH2_SHARE=40
# PL: znacznik czasu ostatniej zmiany kanalu - nie ruszaj recznie.
M2_PLAYERBOT_CH2_SET_AT=0

# Event: Szkatulka Blasku Ksiezyca. Szansa na tysiac, ze zabity potwor upusci
# szkatulke, i osobno dla kamienia Metin. 0 wylacza event. W szkatulce: zwoje
# bonusow, mikstury szybkosci, wzmocnienia, ksiegi - boty otwieraja je same.
# PL: szansa na Szkatulke Blasku Ksiezyca z potwora, w promilach (10 = 1%).
#      Dziala tylko w trakcie wydarzenia ustawionego w panelu.
M2_MOONLIGHT_CHEST_PERMILLE=10
# PL: to samo dla Metinow (300 = 30%). Metiny sypia czesciej niz potwory.
M2_MOONLIGHT_CHEST_STONE_PERMILLE=300

# A legacy Playerbot world may use different names for PID 4..353. The seed
# detects that before changing durable data and, by default, preserves the old
# cohort so the game can still start. Set 1 only for CI or a deliberate
# canonical migration where a mismatch should stop the stack.
# PL: dla testow: 1 = przerwij start, jesli boty w bazie nie zgadzaja sie z
#      oczekiwanymi. Zostaw 0.
PLAYERBOT_SEED_STRICT=0

# Optional protection for an established persistent world. Set this to the
# minimum bot count that must already be present. A mismatch stops startup
# before a fresh Docker daemon/volume can be mistaken for the real server.
# Leave 0 for first installation and public default behaviour.
# PL: dla testow: ilu botow ma juz byc w bazie, zeby start byl uznany za dobry.
PLAYERBOT_EXPECT_MIN_EXISTING_BOTS=0

# How many days of the server's own logs to keep. A busy channel core writes
# roughly 40 MB per hour, so 3 days of one channel is about 8 GB. Lower this
# if your VPS disk is small.
# PL: ile dni logow trzymac. Wiecej dni to wiecej miejsca na dysku, ale latwiej
#      zbadac blad sprzed tygodnia.
M2_LOG_KEEP_DAYS=3

# The database user the server connects as. No reason to change it.
# PL: nazwa uzytkownika bazy, ktorego uzywa serwer. Nie zmieniaj po instalacji.
M2_DB_USER=metin2


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  3b. Updates
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Should the panel find out when a newer version of this project exists?
#
# With this at 1 the panel fetches two text files from the project's repository
# on GitHub, in the background, roughly once a day: the published version
# number, and -- only if it is newer than yours -- the changelog, so it can show
# you what an update would bring. It then says so in the admin area. Players
# never see any of it.
#
# This is the only thing in this entire stack that contacts the internet on its
# own. It means GitHub sees your server's address and the time of the request,
# about once a day, exactly as it would if you opened the project page in a
# browser. Nothing about your server, your players or your database is sent,
# nothing that comes back is ever executed, and no page ever waits for it -- a
# server with no route to the internet behaves identically, it simply never
# finds out that it is behind.
#
# Set it to 0 and the panel contacts nothing at all. Nothing else changes: the
# patch log still shows the changelog of the version you are running.
# PL: czy sprawdzac, czy jest nowa wersja. 1 = tak, 0 = nie.
M2_UPDATE_CHECK=1

# May the panel INSTALL an update, at the press of a button?
#
# Off, and on any server that other people can reach it should stay off. An
# update means running commands on the host machine, and the panel is the part
# of your server that strangers are invited to talk to.
#
# Turning this to 1 is only half of it -- the panel still shows no button
# unless the `updater' service is running, and that service is in a compose
# profile, so it is never started by `docker compose up -d':
#
#     docker compose --profile update up -d updater
#
# The updater is a single shell script in its own tiny container, and it is
# given the host's Docker socket -- which is root on the host. That is the
# whole trade, and it is why this needs two switches instead of one.
#
# UPDATING.md explains what the update does step by step, and what you are
# accepting if you switch this on. Updating by hand is one paste and needs
# neither of these settings.
# PL: czy aktualizowac automatycznie (tylko serwery na Linuksie). 1 = tak,
#      0 = tylko powiadom. Na Windowsie aktualizuje launcher.
M2_UPDATE_APPLY=0

# Where the updater looks, when you have switched it on. On this line it is
# the server folder itself - the one with VERSION, CHANGELOG.md and
# linux-port/ in it - and the update is the package zip from GitHub unpacked
# over it (linux-port/tools/update.sh), never a git checkout: the repository's
# root VERSION belongs to the 1.x line. By hand, from that folder:
#
#     sh linux-port/tools/update.sh
#
# The folder is mounted into the updater container at the same path it has
# on the host, which `docker compose' needs to resolve relative bind mounts.
# PL: gdzie stoi serwer - sciezka wewnatrz kontenera aktualizacji.
M2_UPDATE_STACK_DIR=/opt/metin2
# PL: katalog podreczny aktualizacji.
M2_UPDATE_CACHE_DIR=/var/cache/m2src
# PL: katalog z pobranym repozytorium aktualizacji.
M2_UPDATE_REPO_DIR=/var/cache/m2src/repo
# PL: galaz, z ktorej brac aktualizacje. Zostaw main.
M2_UPDATE_BRANCH=main


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  3c. Playing in the browser
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Off. Leave it off unless you have a browser client to put on the panel.
#
# A browser cannot open a TCP socket, and the game speaks TCP and nothing else,
# so a page that wants to play needs something beside the server that turns a
# WebSocket into a TCP connection. That is the `wsbridge' service. It is in a
# compose profile, so `docker compose up -d' does not start it or build it:
#
#     docker compose --profile browser up -d wsbridge
#
# (install.sh does that for you when this is 1, and stops it again when it is
# not.) The bridge only ever dials the game container, on the game's own ports;
# there is no setting that points it anywhere else, and none that reaches the
# db core.
#
# The other half is the client itself, built to WebAssembly. It is not part of
# these server files -- it is built from game data that is not ours to hand out
# -- and it goes on the panel's volume:
#
#     docker compose cp ./browser panel:/usr/local/m2panel/browser
#
# The panel offers the button only when this is 1 AND that directory has an
# index.html AND the bridge answers. Until all three are true it shows nothing,
# which is better than a button that leads nowhere.
# PL: gra przez przegladarke (eksperyment). 1 = wlacz mostek, 0 = wylacz.
M2_BROWSER_PLAY=0

# The bridge's port on this machine, and which addresses may reach it.
#
# install.sh sets both. With a domain it uses 127.0.0.1, because nginx reaches
# it there and puts it on the panel's own address and certificate -- and that
# is not a preference. The browser client reads the bridge's address out of its
# page URL with a pattern that excludes "/" on purpose, so the bridge can only
# ever be named as host:port and never as a path on this site; and a page
# served over https:// may not open a ws:// connection at all. Together that
# leaves exactly one arrangement behind TLS: this domain, port 443, with nginx
# routing the two prefixes the client uses -- /to/ and /ping -- through to the
# bridge. install.sh writes those. Without a domain the panel is plain HTTP
# anyway and the bridge is published on the port below.
# PL: port mostka do gry przez przegladarke.
M2_BRIDGE_PORT=7789
# PL: adres nasluchu mostka. 127.0.0.1 = tylko ten komputer.
M2_BRIDGE_BIND_ADDRESS=127.0.0.1

# Names this server answers to. The client names a host in every WebSocket URL
# -- that is its protocol -- and the bridge reads it, logs it and throws it
# away: the socket goes to the game container whatever a page asks for, which
# is what makes an open proxy impossible here rather than merely unlikely.
# Filled in, this additionally REFUSES a name the server does not go by; empty
# (the default) accepts any name and still dials only the game. Empty is right
# for most servers: a public address changes, and a client that named the old
# one has still reached the right box.
# PL: dodatkowe nazwy hosta, pod ktorymi mostek ma odpowiadac.
M2_BRIDGE_HOST_ALIASES=

# Believe X-Forwarded-For. Only ever 1 when nothing but nginx can reach the
# bridge (the address above is 127.0.0.1) -- otherwise anyone can claim any
# address and the per-player connection limit means nothing. Set to 0 and,
# behind nginx, every player counts as the same one.
# PL: 1, gdy mostek stoi za nginx/Cloudflare i ma czytac prawdziwy adres gracza.
M2_BRIDGE_TRUST_PROXY=0

# How many browser connections at once, in total and per player. A player uses
# one for the login server and one for the channel, and briefly two channels
# while changing.
# PL: ile polaczen naraz mostek przyjmie.
M2_BRIDGE_MAX_CONNECTIONS=200
# PL: ile polaczen z jednego adresu IP.
M2_BRIDGE_MAX_PER_IP=8

# Which pages may connect. Empty means any, and that is the honest default:
# these game ports are published to the internet for the downloaded client
# regardless, so refusing a foreign page here would protect nothing. Fill it in
# (e.g. https://example.org) on a server where that is not true.
# PL: z jakich stron wolno laczyc sie do mostka. Puste = bez ograniczen.
M2_BRIDGE_ORIGINS=


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  4. Advanced -- you will probably never touch these
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# What the cores bind their listening sockets to. 0.0.0.0 means every
# interface, which is what a container wants. Verified working: the cores log
#   BIND_IP: 0.0.0.0 -> listening on every interface (PUBLIC_IP left at ...)
# and their sockets appear on 0.0.0.0. Leave this alone.
# PL: adres, na ktorym nasluchuja rdzenie gry wewnatrz kontenera.
M2_BIND_IP=0.0.0.0

# Enables the server's test-server behaviour (verbose logs, some checks off).
# PL: 1 wlacza tryb testowy silnika (komendy GM dla wszystkich). Zostaw 0 na
#      serwerze, na ktorym ktos gra.
M2_TEST_SERVER=0

# Suffix appended to every game table name. Only for running two servers off
# one database, which is not what this stack is for.
# PL: przyrostek nazw tabel w bazie. Zostaw puste.
M2_TABLE_POSTFIX=

# Password for the server's built-in admin text page. Unrelated to the panel.
# PL: haslo strony administracyjnej silnika.
M2_ADMINPAGE_PASSWORD=

# Write a core dump when a core crashes. Off by default: a game core is ~320 MB
# resident, so a crash loop fills a small VPS disk within minutes. Turn on only
# while investigating a crash.
# PL: 1 = zapisuj zrzuty pamieci po awarii rdzenia. Przydatne przy zglaszaniu
#      bledu, zajmuje miejsce.
M2_CORE_DUMPS=0

# How many inventory slots the panel searches for a free space. r40250 gives a
# character four pages of 45. Set this to 45 and the panel only ever looks at
# the first page, and tells you the inventory is full when three pages are empty.
# PL: ile komorek ma plecak postaci. 180 to cztery strony.
M2_INVENTORY_SLOTS=180

# The largest stack the panel will write into player.item.count. That column is
# TINYINT UNSIGNED, so 255 is the hard ceiling -- ask for more and MySQL stores
# 255 without reporting anything.
# PL: najwiekszy stos przedmiotow, jaki silnik obsluzy.
M2_MAX_ITEM_COUNT=255

# Set to 1 only when this server is reachable from nowhere but the machine it
# runs on -- what the Windows installer builds, and what `install.sh --local`
# builds. The panel then tells you plainly that nobody else can join, instead
# of telling you to hand the address out to players.
#
# Leave it at 0 for a real server, INCLUDING one behind nginx with a domain.
# The panel binds to 127.0.0.1 in that case too, which is exactly why this is a
# separate setting rather than something the panel tries to work out itself.
# PL: 1 = caly serwer tylko dla tego komputera (nikt z sieci nie wejdzie).
M2_LOCAL_ONLY=0

# Interface on which Docker publishes the auth and game ports.
# Use 127.0.0.1 for an offline/single-player installation and 0.0.0.0 only
# when intentionally accepting game connections from other computers.
# PL: na jakim adresie komputera wystawic porty gry. 127.0.0.1 = tylko ty,
#      0.0.0.0 = takze gracze z sieci. Przycisk COOP ustawia to sam.
M2_HOST_BIND_ADDRESS=0.0.0.0

# Interface on which Docker publishes the admin panel. Keep this separate from
# M2_PANEL_PUBLIC_PORT: the latter must contain digits only (for example 7788),
# never an address-and-port string such as 127.0.0.1:7788. A domain/nginx or
# local-only installation should use 127.0.0.1 here.
# PL: to samo dla paneli. 127.0.0.1 trzyma panel przy tym komputerze.
M2_PANEL_BIND_ADDRESS=0.0.0.0

# Which ports the panel probes to decide whether the game is up.
# PL: porty, ktore panel odpytuje, sprawdzajac, czy serwer zyje.
M2_PANEL_STATUS_PORTS=11000,13000

# Build-time only. Leave empty to use every core the build machine has.
# PL: ile rdzeni procesora uzyc przy budowaniu serwera. Puste = policz z
#      pamieci maszyny (na 8 GB build z wieloma zadaniami potrafi zawisnac).
M2_MAKE_JOBS=
# Strip debug symbols from the binaries. 1 makes the image ~60 MB smaller;
# set to 0 if you intend to debug a crash with gdb.
# PL: 1 = mniejsze pliki wykonywalne, 0 = zostaw symbole do czytania awarii.
M2_STRIP_BINARIES=1
# PL: obraz systemu, na ktorym budowany jest serwer. Nie zmieniaj bez potrzeby.
M2_BASE_IMAGE=ubuntu:24.04
# A launcher-generated, persistent installation identity. It lets a freshly
# unpacked copy use its own containers and volumes instead of accidentally
# attaching to another Metin2 installation on the same PC. Leave blank; the
# Windows launcher fills both values on first start and stores the identity in
# .m2install.json beside the launcher.
# PL: nazwa projektu Dockera dla tej instalacji - wpisuje ja launcher. Reczna
#      zmiana odetnie serwer od jego wlasnych danych.
M2_COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=
# PL: przedrostek nazw kontenerow - jak wyzej, ustawia launcher.
M2_CONTAINER_PREFIX=

# Shinsoo and Jinno. 1 (the default since 2.0.8) seeds all three kingdoms and
# lets each core start its own on maps 1, 21 and 41; the bot count is split
# equally between them. 0 keeps the Chunjo cohort alone. The launcher switches
# an older .env from 0 to 1 once and records that in the key below; set 0 again
# after that and it stays 0.
# Since 2.0.12 the game cores read this switch too: a 0 starts no Shinsoo or
# Jinno bot even on a world that once seeded them (they stay in the database).
# PL: 1 = boty we wszystkich trzech krolestwach, 0 = tylko Chunjo.
M2_PLAYERBOT_KINGDOMS=1
# PL: znacznik, ze powyzsze zostalo juz raz ustawione - nie ruszaj recznie.
M2_PLAYERBOT_KINGDOMS_DEFAULTED=1

# Jak swiat jest rozlozony na trzy rdzenie gry.
#
#   split   - domyslnie i bez zmian: kazde krolestwo na wlasnym rdzeniu, pelna
#             rownoleglosc. Caly front (Dolina Orkow, Pustynia, Sohan, Lochy
#             Pajakow) hostuje rdzen Chunjo, a bot nie ma klienta, wiec nie
#             przechodzi miedzy rdzeniami - Shinsoo i Jinno koncza na ~36 lvl.
#   unified - mapy wszystkich trzech krolestw i front na jednym rdzeniu, wiec
#             kazdy bot moze wyjsc na front. Koszt: caly swiat tyka na jednym
#             rdzeniu (zmierzone przy 1500 botach: 9,4 s z 60). Dla rozsadnej
#             populacji na jednej maszynie; przy 2500+ zostaw split.
#
# Doszlo w 2.0.30 i az do 2.0.31 tej linii nie bylo w .env.example, wiec nikt,
# kto aktualizowal zamiast instalowac od nowa, nie mial czego przelaczyc
# (NerrVoVy, 13 wrzesnia) - Compose mial swoj wlasny domyslny split, wiec nic
# sie nie psulo, tylko nie dalo sie wlaczyc. Od 2.0.85 domyslne jest unified,
# a starsze instalacje sa przelaczane raz (M2_PLAYERBOT_WORLD_LAYOUT_DEFAULTED),
# chyba ze swiat prosi o wiecej niz 1500 botow - tam zostaje split.
# PL: uklad swiata. unified = wszystkie krolestwa i caly front na jednym
#      rdzeniu, wiec boty Shinsoo i Jinno nie koncza na 36 poziomie.
#      split = trzy rdzenie, szybsze przy bardzo duzej liczbie botow
#      (powyzej 1500), ale dwa krolestwa nie maja gdzie rosnac.
M2_PLAYERBOT_WORLD_LAYOUT=unified

# Poziom trudnosci swiata - ile gracz czeka u Biologa i u Stajennego, i ile
# gracze oraz boty czekaja miedzy dwiema ksiegami tej samej umiejetnosci.
# Biologa i Stajennego botow to nie dotyczy (nigdy nie czekali).
#
#   easy   - domyslnie: bez czekania (tak dziala kazdy swiat od 2.0.55/2.0.56).
#   medium - jedna trzecia oryginalu: Biolog 8 h, kucyk i kazda Ksiega Konia
#            4 h, trening konia medalami 6 h (poziomy 1-10) i 7 h (11-19),
#            ksiegi umiejetnosci 7 h (gracze i boty).
#   hard   - jak w pakiecie: Biolog 24 h, kucyk i Ksiegi Konia 12 h, treningi
#            18 h (1-10) i 21 h (11-19), ksiegi umiejetnosci 21 h.
#   custom - godziny z linii ponizej: Biolog, (jedna liczba) kazde czekanie
#            u Stajennego i ksiegi - osobno gracze, osobno boty. Ulamki
#            dozwolone (0.5 = pol godziny).
#
# Czytane przy starcie serwera (migrator zapisuje flagi zdarzen, questy i gra
# je czytaja), wiec zmiana wymaga restartu. Launcher ma do tego przycisk.
# Panel WWW (Mnozniki serwera -> Poziom trudnosci) zmienia to samo od razu;
# taka zmiana zostaje, dopoki nie zmienisz trudnosci tutaj albo w launcherze.
# PL: trudnosc swiata: easy, medium, hard albo custom. Ustawia czasy oczekiwania
#      u Biologa, u Stajennego i na kolejna ksiege. easy = bez czekania.
M2_DIFFICULTY=easy
# PL: ile godzin czekac miedzy oddaniami u Biologa (dziala przy M2_DIFFICULTY=custom).
M2_BIOLOGIST_WAIT_HOURS=0
# PL: ile godzin czekac na konia u Stajennego (jak wyzej).
M2_HORSE_WAIT_HOURS=0
# PL: ile godzin gracz czeka miedzy dwiema ksiegami tej samej umiejetnosci
#      (jak wyzej). 0 = kolejna ksiega od razu. Zwoj Egzorcyzmu pomija czekanie.
M2_BOOK_WAIT_HOURS=0
# PL: to samo dla botow (jak wyzej). 0 = boty czytaja od razu.
M2_BOT_BOOK_WAIT_HOURS=0

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  mt2009 build only (rendered by linux-port-mt2009/port/envify.py)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The Ubuntu package mirror the image build installs from. Empty means the
# Gdansk mirror (http://ubuntu.task.gda.pl/ubuntu/), which is fast from Poland;
# Ubuntu's own archive.ubuntu.com served a few kilobytes a second here on the
# day 2.0 came out and every first build sat at deps 7/7 for twenty minutes.
# Another country wants a closer mirror, e.g. http://mirrors.edge.kernel.org/ubuntu/
# or http://archive.ubuntu.com/ubuntu/ for the official one.
# PL: serwer lustrzany pakietow uzywany przy budowaniu. Puste = polski (szybki
#      z Polski). Zmien, jesli budowa stoi na pobieraniu pakietow.
M2_APT_MIRROR=

# How much faster than the original game experience, item drops and yang come
# in, as percentages - 100 is exactly how the game was made. These three are
# read ONLY at the first start of a fresh world (and after a world reset): the
# migrator writes the event flags from them before the cores let the first bot
# in. A world that has had them once changes them from the panel's "Stawki"
# page alone, which is where they then live; editing this file after that does
# nothing. The launcher asks for them when it resets a world or installs one.
# PL: mnozniki swiezego swiata w procentach - doswiadczenie, drop, yang.
#      100 = jak w oryginalnej grze. Uzywane tylko przy pierwszym starcie
#      nowego swiata; potem zmienia sie je na stronie "Stawki" w panelu.
M2_RATE_EXP=100
M2_RATE_DROP=100
M2_RATE_YANG=100

# The world comes up, the bots wait at the door: 1 means not one bot is in the
# world after a start until the operator lets them in, from the panel's AI page
# or from the launcher. Until then the rates, the respawns and the personalities
# can be set with nothing happening in the world. The launcher offers this when
# it resets a world; off by default.
# PL: 1 = po starcie w swiecie nie ma ani jednego bota, dopoki nie wpuscisz ich
#      przyciskiem w panelu (strona AI) albo w launcherze. Daje czas na
#      ustawienie stawek i respawnow, zanim cokolwiek sie zacznie dziac.
M2_PLAYERBOT_START_HELD=0

# Whether a player's new character gets the apprentice chest (Skrzynia Ucznia,
# the chest chain the bots carry) at its first login: 1 on, 0 off. The launcher
# asks when it makes a world; a change reaches the game at the next start.
# PL: 1 = nowa postac gracza dostaje Skrzynie Ucznia przy pierwszym logowaniu,
#      0 = nie dostaje. Launcher pyta o to przy tworzeniu swiata; zmiana
#      dziala od nastepnego startu serwera.
M2_STARTER_CHEST=1
